.TH QFW-SRUN 1 "August 2026" "QFw 0.1.0" "QFw Commands"
.SH NAME
qfw-srun \- launch an application in a prepared QFw runtime
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B qfw-srun
.RI [ options ]
.I application
.RI [ arguments ... ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B qfw-srun
loads the environment recorded by
.BR qfw-setup (1),
configures the application DEFw client, and launches the requested application
through
.BR defw-python .
The application may be a Python script or another command accepted by that
wrapper.
.PP
Without
.BR --run-dir ,
the current application runtime is used. Several application steps may use the
same prepared runtime before
.BR qfw-teardown (1).
.PP
In a heterogeneous Slurm allocation, the application defaults to group 0.
Application-owned directory, QPM, and simulator services are placed separately
by setup according to the runtime profile.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --run-dir " directory"
Use an explicit prepared application run directory.
.TP
.BI --nodes " count"
Pass a node count to the generated Slurm launch.
.TP
.BI --ntasks " count"
Pass a task count to the generated Slurm launch.
.TP
.BI --nodelist " hosts"
Restrict the generated Slurm launch to these hosts.
.TP
.BI --het-group " number"
Select an explicit heterogeneous group. Group 0 is the default.
.TP
.B --exclusive
Request an exclusive Slurm step.
.SH EXIT STATUS
The application or Slurm step exit status is returned. An incomplete or
missing runtime returns nonzero without launching the application.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR qfw-setup (1),
.BR qfw-status (1),
.BR qfw-teardown (1),
.BR qfw-activate (1),
.BR qfw (7)
